 ```
 
+### 5. Rank-1 LoRA adapters (`--lora`, e.g. the "Uncensored" abliteration)
+Every mode takes `--lora <adapter.gguf>`: an `inkling2_loop` rank-1 LoRA GGUF with
+`blk.N.attn_output.weight.lora_{a,b}`, `blk.N.ffn_down_exps.weight.lora_{a,b}` (per expert)
+and `token_embd.weight.lora_{a,b}` for all 24 layers (98 tensors, e.g. AtomicChat
+`Inkling-2-Mini-Uncensored-LoRA.gguf`).  `W' = W + (alpha/rank) B A` is applied at run time in
+the existing epilogues of every path (decode graph, batched MTP verify, multi-slot batch,
+WMMA prefill, the DSpark drafter's anchor embedding), on every loop visit; the quantised
+weights are untouched.  Without `--lora` the launch sequence and every result are unchanged.
+```bash
+./build/nib serve -m models/Inkling-2-Mini-NVFP4-Mixed.gguf --mtp models/mtp.safetensors \
+  --lora models/Inkling-2-Mini-Uncensored-LoRA.gguf
+# CPU-only check of the adapter against the pack and of the kernel arithmetic:
+./build/nib-lora-check models/Inkling-2-Mini-NVFP4-Mixed.gguf models/Inkling-2-Mini-Uncensored-LoRA.gguf
+```
+The LoRA terms live in the default kernels only, so `--lora` refuses the A/B switches that select
+other wo / MoE kernels (`--wo-v3`, `--fdot2-wo`, `--fuse-wob`, `--moe-ship-fused` != 2, `--moe-*-v3`,
+`--fdot2-moe`, `--moe-q8-fused`, `--fdot2-q8moe`).
+
